\f0\fs32 \cf0 The purpose of this macro is to use StarDist to count nuclei in wholemount and section CZIs.\
\
\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\
\
Preparations:\
\'97Download the PTBIOP plugin\
\
\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\
\
In this folder, I\'92ve included 3 versions of the macro:\
\
For both 1 and 2, you are required to first choose a directory to draw expt/cntl ROIs from (Wholemount_RoiSet). You are then asked to choose a folder to draw stardist outputs from (Wholemount_STARDISTSET).\
\'97\
In 2 only, you will then be asked to choose a folder to save output ROIs - afterward where to save output CSVs.\
***I have no \'93wait for user\'94 lines because they crashed fiji for me\
\
\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\'97\
\
1. StardistROI_Overlap_base.ijm  \'97  closest to the base macro - requires a tif image and a prepared folder of both the ROIs generated by Stardist, and also the experimental/control ROIs we\'92ve drawn ourselves.\
\
-\'93Practice Image,\'94 Wholemount_RoiSet, Wholemount_STARDISTSET, (STARDISTSET.zip,RoiSet.zip) are used with this macro. \
-
\f1\b Has no output
\f0\b0 . Only lists all the Stardist ROIs within the experimental and control ROIs in the ROI manager, but does not distinguish between expt/cntl.\
\
2. StardistROI_Overlap_EXPTvsCNTL.ijm  \'97  Like StardistROI_Overlap_base.ijm, requires a pre-made set of stardist and expt/cntl ROI folders. Unlike StardistROI_Overlap_base.ijm, this version generates separate expt/cntl csvs and separate expt/cntl ROIs - which are saved to the \'93example folders\'94 as \'93PRACTICE IMAGE\'85\'94\
\
-\'93Practice Image,\'94 Wholemount_RoiSet, Wholemount_STARDISTSET, (STARDISTSET.zip,RoiSet.zip) are used with this macro. \
\
3. StardistROI_Overlap_EXPTvsCNTL_Local.ijm  \'97  This macro does not require any premade ROIs. Only a CZI needs to be open when this program is run. \
\
\'97Has similar outputs as StardistROI_Overlap_EXPTvsCNTL.ijm, but control and experimental ROIs are drawn during runtime (\'93locally\'94). \
-Requires defining a NC channel\
-Asks first for a folder to save ROIs, then a folder to save Csvs.\
-Has not yet been super optimized, so might be inefficiencies that take up computational resources, etc.\
\
- Uses either CZI in the folder: \
	-20240110_ApoDMO1,0mM_BF;SOX10;ApoDMO;Pax7;DAPI_Emb1_10ss_10x_stack.czi\
	-20240910_BRECtrlMOvBRERFTN2MO;1.0mM_BF;Sox9;H2BRFP;eGFP;DAPI_Emb08_7ss_20xstack_section10.czi\
-outputs end with \'93CntlNCROIs,\'94 \'93ExptNCROIs,\'94 or \'93largeNCROIs\'94\
\
